2014-08-07 5:11 GMT+04:00 TR NS <transfire@gmail.com>:

> Why are there so many "end-whatever" cmavo? We can't close any open
> clauses until we've closed that most recent one, correct? So why not just
> have one "end current clause" cmavo?
>
> .trans.
>

This is mostly true. In my style out of terminators (particles that close
constructs) I use mostly {vau}, {li'u} or {le'u} (for closing quotations),
{ku} only after modals.

So yes, of course, you can use a style where most terminators are not used.


